it policy do you take  responsibility for the policy actually  brexit secretary that Lisa Nandi has  just described as a disaster I take  responsibility for everything in our  manifesto it was actually a Shadow  Cabinet decision it was actually  decision our whole party a party  conference but I'm not going to shirk  from that but I do there's a there's a  since we're looking at what happens next  leave remain is over so that divide is  not there we've left the EU so whether  you were full remain or leave is  irrelevant but there's a big test coming  up for all of us okay because we had a  problem cuz the question is now Johnson  is heading for no deal or nearly no deal  if we become leader of the Labour Party  will we take him on or we will give in  to it and that's the question we need to  answer okay Kirsten we just said that  the Shadow Cabinet was responsible for  Labour's brexit policy as so on in the  chair cabinet do you see yourselves as  equally responsible look I think we need  to recognize that there were many  reasons as to why we lost this general  election and brexit was one of the key  ones I come from a leave constituency  and I could feel the anger on the  doorstep from my constituents they saw  rose in Parliament playing parliamentary  games they didn't understand why and  they thought we were trying to attempt  to overturn the result of the referendum  and if you were a strong remain  supporter well he didn't think we were  going far enough in having that close  relationship with the European Union  well the sad fact is is that with that  lack of trust in Breck see it took so  many other things down with it and yes  leadership did come up on the doorstep  because we'd had four years of Jeremy  being vilified and attacked by the press  we knew that we weren't trusted on  issues such as anti-semitism and our  handling of that within the party and on  our manifesto the sad thing is is that  despite it being the most transformative  manifesto we've h